Z||000007||fierodave||03-30-2000||05:44 PM||||Checks and credit cards are fine!!!!!!!  there as good as the people that use them!!!!!<P>this is a case of the guy seemed cool needed help, and I purchased an engine for him,  he never made a payment  now is email is dead and his phone is not working.  I found the engine( I did not have it)  and sent the money to the engine owner,  He went and picked it up from that guy , installed it, and even thanked me on the list for my help.  <BR>this has nothing to do with bad service, or bad checks!  It's just no payment on an item I didn't even stock at that time,  and me being to nice a guy!(DUMB)  Like I said,  OH WELL!  this will not affect the people that have gotten stuff from me in the past.<BR>Thanks for the space<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000008||Motorhead||03-30-2000||06:43 PM||||Hey Dave, I purchased some stuff and used something called pay-pal.  Worked great. Basically I opened an account, deposited funds into that account using a credit card, then deposited funds for the goods I was purchasing into the recipiants account.  No preblems.  Seller got his money within minutes, and I didn't have to buy, then mail a money order, wait for the MO to arrive then wait for the goods to arrive.  Had it in my hands within 3 days of ordering.<P>You might check it out.<P>Mike||||reg||1
